# Responsive Fixture

## Overview

Clean Professional favors clarity over decoration: generous whitespace, high-contrast neutrals, and a single confident accent for action.
**Personality:** Professional, calm, trustworthy.
**Audience:** Product teams shipping web applications.
**Direction:** Clean, spacious, high-contrast neutrals with a single accent.
**Mood:** professional, clean, modern, accessible

## Colors

A high-contrast neutral foundation with a single blue accent reserved for primary action and focus.

- **Primary (#2563EB):** primary color token.
- **Secondary (#475569):** secondary color token.
- **Neutral (#0F172A):** neutral color token.
- **Surface (#FFFFFF):** surface color token.
- **On Surface (#0F172A):** on-surface color token.
- **Muted (#64748B):** muted color token.
- **Border (#E2E8F0):** border color token.
- **Error (#DC2626):** error color token.
- **Success (#16A34A):** success color token.

## Typography

Inter across the board; weight and size carry hierarchy, not color.

- **Headline Lg:** Inter 32px/1.15, weight 700.
- **Headline Md:** Inter 24px/1.2, weight 600.
- **Body Lg:** Inter 18px/1.6, weight 400.
- **Body Md:** Inter 16px/1.6, weight 400.
- **Body Sm:** Inter 14px/1.5, weight 400.
- **Label Md:** Inter 14px/1.2, weight 500.

## Layout

A 12-column grid on a strict 8px spacing rhythm; content caps at 1200px.

A 12-column grid; content caps at 1200px.

| Step | Value |
|---|---|
| base | 16px |
| xs | 4px |
| sm | 8px |
| md | 16px |
| lg | 24px |
| xl | 40px |
| 2xl | 64px |

## Elevation & Depth

Depth comes from subtle, tight shadows on raised surfaces rather than heavy drop shadows.

| Level | box-shadow |
|---|---|
| sm | \`0 1px 2px 0 rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05)\` |
| md | \`0 4px 6px -1px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.1)\` |
| lg | \`0 10px 15px -3px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.1)\` |

## Shapes

Soft 8px corners on interactive elements; pills only for badges and avatars.

| Level | Radius |
|---|---|
| none | 0 |
| sm | 4px |
| md | 8px |
| lg | 12px |
| full | 9999px |

## Components

### Button
A clickable action trigger. Primary drives the single most important action per view.
**Variants:** primary, secondary  
**Sizes:** sm, md, lg  
**States:** default, hover, focus, disabled, loading
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| tablet | 768px | visible | comfortable padding | paddingX: {spacing.lg} |
| desktop | 1024px | visible | wider hit target | paddingX: {spacing.xl}; paddingY: {spacing.md} |
**Do**
- Use one primary button per view.
- Show a spinner in the loading state.
**Don't**
- Don't use inline hex — reference color tokens.

### Input
A single-line text field with label, helper text, and error states.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** md  
**States:** default, focus, disabled, error

## Do's and Don'ts

- Do reserve the primary color for the single most important action per screen.
- Do maintain WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1 for body text).
- Don't mix more than two font weights in one view.
- Don't hard-code hex values — reference tokens.
"
`;

exports[`golden — Flutter stack > SKILL.md Flutter section (prefixed-class) 1`] = `
"### Flutter

- Tokens live in \`lib/theme/\` (\`app_colors.dart\`, \`app_typography.dart\`, \`app_spacing.dart\`, \`app_theme.dart\`) as static members of namespace classes (\`AppColors\`, \`AppTypography\`, \`AppSpacing\`, \`AppRadius\`, \`AppBorders\`, \`AppShadows\`, \`AppBreakpoints\`).
- Reference them by name, e.g. color \`AppColors.primary\`, text style \`AppTypography.headlineLg\`, spacing \`AppSpacing.base\`.
- Never write \`Color(0xFF...)\` inline — reference the token constant. Inline colors are drift and are auto-fixed to the constant.
- Install the theme once: \`MaterialApp(theme: AppTheme.light, darkTheme: AppTheme.dark)\`. For colors that must follow light/dark, read \`Theme.of(context).colorScheme\` rather than a light-mode constant.
- Responsive layout uses \`LayoutBuilder\` and compares \`constraints.maxWidth\` to the breakpoint constants (e.g. \`AppBreakpoints.tablet\`) — no media queries.
- Component stubs live in \`lib/widgets/{ComponentName}/{component_name}.dart\`; add behavior there without re-styling them.

"
`;

exports[`golden — Flutter stack > SKILL.md Flutter section (raw) 1`] = `
"### Flutter

- Tokens live in \`lib/theme/\` (\`app_colors.dart\`, \`app_typography.dart\`, \`app_spacing.dart\`, \`app_theme.dart\`) as top-level \`k\`-prefixed constants (\`kColor…\`, \`kText…\`, \`kSpacing…\`, \`kRadius…\`, \`kBreakpoint…\`).
- Reference them by name, e.g. color \`kColorPrimary\`, text style \`kTextHeadlineLg\`, spacing \`kSpacingBase\`.
- Never write \`Color(0xFF...)\` inline — reference the token constant. Inline colors are drift and are auto-fixed to the constant.
- Install the theme once: \`MaterialApp(theme: AppTheme.light, darkTheme: AppTheme.dark)\`. For colors that must follow light/dark, read \`Theme.of(context).colorScheme\` rather than a light-mode constant.
- Responsive layout uses \`LayoutBuilder\` and compares \`constraints.maxWidth\` to the breakpoint constants (e.g. \`kBreakpointTablet\`) — no media queries.
- Component stubs live in \`lib/widgets/{ComponentName}/{component_name}.dart\`; add behavior there without re-styling them.

"
`;

exports[`golden — Flutter stack > SKILL.md Flutter section (snake_const) 1`] = `
"### Flutter

- Tokens live in \`lib/theme/\` (\`app_colors.dart\`, \`app_typography.dart\`, \`app_spacing.dart\`, \`app_theme.dart\`) as top-level group-prefixed constants (\`c_\`, \`t_\`, \`s_\`, \`r_\`, \`bw_\`, \`sh_\`, \`bp_\`).
- Reference them by name, e.g. color \`c_primary\`, text style \`t_headline_lg\`, spacing \`s_base\`.
- Never write \`Color(0xFF...)\` inline — reference the token constant. Inline colors are drift and are auto-fixed to the constant.
- Install the theme once: \`MaterialApp(theme: AppTheme.light, darkTheme: AppTheme.dark)\`. For colors that must follow light/dark, read \`Theme.of(context).colorScheme\` rather than a light-mode constant.
- Responsive layout uses \`LayoutBuilder\` and compares \`constraints.maxWidth\` to the breakpoint constants (e.g. \`bp_tablet\`) — no media queries.
- Component stubs live in \`lib/widgets/{ComponentName}/{component_name}.dart\`; add behavior there without re-styling them.

"
`;

exports[`golden — React components > default schema 1`] = `
[
  {
    "content": "// Generated by design-spec — do not edit by hand.
// Source of truth: design-spec.schema.json. Run \`design-spec compile\` to regenerate.

import React from 'react'

export type ButtonVariant = 'primary' | 'secondary'

export interface ButtonProps extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement> {
  variant?: ButtonVariant
  size?: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg'
  disabled?: boolean
  loading?: boolean
}

const base = 'bg-primary text-surface text-label-md rounded-md px-md py-sm'

const variants: Record<ButtonVariant, string> = {
  primary: '',
  secondary: 'bg-surface text-primary border-border border-thin',
}

export function Button({ variant = 'primary', children, className, ...props }: ButtonProps) {
  const classes = [base, variants[variant], className].filter(Boolean).join(' ')
  return <button className={classes} {...props}>{children}</button>
}
",
    "filename": "components/react-tailwind/Button.tsx",
    "language": "tsx",
  },
  {
    "content": "// Generated by design-spec — do not edit by hand.
// Source of truth: design-spec.schema.json. Run \`design-spec compile\` to regenerate.

import React from 'react'

export interface InputProps extends React.InputHTMLAttributes<HTMLInputElement> {
  label?: string
  placeholder?: string
  disabled?: boolean
  error?: string
}

const base = 'bg-surface text-on-surface text-body-md border-border border-thin rounded-md px-md py-sm'

export function Input({ className, ...props }: InputProps) {
  const classes = [base, className].filter(Boolean).join(' ')
  return <input className={classes} {...props} />
}
",
    "filename": "components/react-tailwind/Input.tsx",
    "language": "tsx",
  },
]
`;

