---

# Tier 2 Fixture

## Overview

Clean Professional favors clarity over decoration: generous whitespace, high-contrast neutrals, and a single confident accent for action.
**Personality:** Professional, calm, trustworthy.
**Audience:** Product teams shipping web applications.
**Direction:** Clean, spacious, high-contrast neutrals with a single accent.
**Mood:** professional, clean, modern, accessible

## Colors

A high-contrast neutral foundation with a single blue accent reserved for primary action and focus.

- **Primary (#3B6EF5):** primary color token.
- **Surface Default (#FFFFFF):** surface-default color token.
- **Surface Raised (#F1F5F9):** surface-raised color token.
- **Surface Overlay (#E2E8F0):** surface-overlay color token.
- **Surface Sunken (#F0F4F8):** surface-sunken color token.
- **Surface Border (#E2E8F0):** surface-border color token.
- **Surface Border Subtle (#F1F5F9):** surface-border-subtle color token.
- **On Surface (#0F172A):** on-surface color token.
- **On Surface Muted (#475569):** on-surface-muted color token.
- **On Surface Subtle (#94A3B8):** on-surface-subtle color token.
- **On Primary (#FFFFFF):** on-primary color token.
- **Status Error (#EF4444):** status-error color token.
- **Status Warning (#F59E0B):** status-warning color token.
- **Status Info (#3B82F6):** status-info color token.
- **Status Error Surface (#FEF2F2):** status-error-surface color token.
- **Status Warning Surface (#FFFBEB):** status-warning-surface color token.
- **Status Info Surface (#EFF6FF):** status-info-surface color token.

## Typography

Inter across the board; weight and size carry hierarchy, not color.

- **Display Md:** Inter 40px/1.1, weight 700.
- **Headline Sm:** Inter 20px/1.3, weight 600.
- **Body Md:** Inter 16px/1.5, weight 400.
- **Body Sm:** Inter 14px/1.5, weight 400.
- **Label Lg:** Inter 16px/1.25, weight 500.
- **Label Md:** Inter 14px/1.25, weight 500.
- **Label Sm:** Inter 12px/1.25, weight 500.

## Layout

A 12-column grid on a strict 8px spacing rhythm; content caps at 1200px.

A 12-column grid; content caps at 1200px.

| Step | Value |
|---|---|
| xs | 4px |
| sm | 8px |
| md | 16px |
| lg | 24px |
| xl | 32px |
| 2xl | 48px |

## Elevation & Depth

Depth comes from subtle, tight shadows on raised surfaces rather than heavy drop shadows.

| Level | box-shadow |
|---|---|
| sm | \`0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.10), 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)\` |
| xl | \`0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.10), 0 8px 10px -6px rgba(0,0,0,0.10)\` |

## Shapes

Soft 8px corners on interactive elements; pills only for badges and avatars.

| Level | Radius |
|---|---|
| sm | 4px |
| md | 6px |
| lg | 10px |
| xl | 16px |
| full | 9999px |

## Components

### Navbar
Top navigation bar with brand, links, and actions. Links collapse behind a menu toggle on small screens.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** default, menu-open
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | Links render inline and the menu toggle is hidden; below md the links collapse behind the toggle. | paddingX: {spacing.lg} |
**Do**
- Mark the current page link with aria-current="page"
- Give the menu toggle aria-expanded + aria-controls
**Don't**
- Don't hide primary navigation on mobile without a toggle

### Sidebar
Vertical navigation. One-level (flat) or multilevel (nested, collapsible groups). Collapses to an icon rail on small screens.
**Variants:** one-level, multilevel  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** default, collapsed
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | Expanded rail with labels; below md the sidebar collapses to an icon rail. | — |
**Do**
- Toggle nested groups with a button carrying aria-expanded
- Keep labels available as tooltips or aria-label when collapsed
**Don't**
- Don't nest deeper than two levels

### Tabs
Switches between related panels in place. Line, pill, or contained; horizontal or vertical.
**Variants:** line, pill, contained  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** default, hover, selected, disabled
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | Vertical orientation is honored; below md tabs are one horizontal row that scrolls. | — |
**Do**
- Use role="tablist" / "tab" / "tabpanel" with aria-selected and aria-controls
- Move between tabs with the arrow keys
**Don't**
- Don't use tabs for sequential steps — use a stepper

### Breadcrumbs
Hierarchical trail to the current page, with a tokenized separator.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** default, hover
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | Full trail; below md the middle crumbs collapse to an ellipsis. | — |
**Do**
- Wrap in <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"> and mark the last item aria-current="page"
**Don't**
- Don't link the current page

### Pagination
Numbered page links with previous / next controls.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** sm, md  
**States:** default, hover, current, disabled
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | Numbered pages; below md only previous / next with "Page x of y". | — |
**Do**
- Wrap in <nav aria-label="Pagination">; mark the current page aria-current="page"
- Give prev/next an aria-label
**Don't**
- Don't render more than 7 page slots — use an ellipsis

### Accordion
Stacked disclosure sections. Single or multiple open; height animates unless reduced motion is set.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** collapsed, expanded, disabled
**Do**
- Make each trigger a <button> with aria-expanded and aria-controls
- Respect prefers-reduced-motion
**Don't**
- Don't hide content a user must read to finish a task

### Progress
Progress bar. Determinate shows a value; indeterminate shows ongoing work with no known end.
**Variants:** determinate, indeterminate  
**Sizes:** sm, md  
**States:** default, complete
**Do**
- Use role="progressbar" with aria-valuenow/min/max; omit aria-valuenow when indeterminate
**Don't**
- Don't animate the indeterminate bar when reduced motion is requested

### EmptyState
Placeholder for a view with no content yet: icon, title, description, and a next action.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** default
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | — | padding: {spacing.2xl} |
**Do**
- Explain why the view is empty and offer one clear next step
**Don't**
- Don't show an empty state while data is still loading — use a skeleton

### ErrorState
Full-view error: not found (404), server error (500), or no permission (403), with a recovery action.
**Variants:** not-found, server-error, forbidden  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** default
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | — | padding: {spacing.2xl} |
**Do**
- Say what happened in plain words and offer a way out
**Don't**
- Don't show stack traces or internal error ids to end users

### Table
Tabular data with sortable headers, row selection, and a pagination slot. Rows stack into cards on small screens.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** —  
**States:** default, row-hover, row-selected, sorted
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | Full table; below md each row stacks into a label / value card. | — |
**Do**
- Put aria-sort on the sorted header; make sort controls buttons
- Label each row checkbox with the row name
**Don't**
- Don't use a table for layout

### Drawer
Panel that slides in from the left, right, or bottom over an overlay. Becomes a bottom sheet on small screens.
**Variants:** default  
**Sizes:** sm, md, lg  
**States:** open, closed
**Responsive**

| Breakpoint | Min-width | Visibility | Layout | Overrides |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| md | 768px | visible | Side panel from the chosen edge; below md it renders as a bottom sheet. | — |
**Do**
- Use role="dialog" with an accessible name; move focus in on open and restore it on close
- Close on Escape and overlay click
**Don't**
- Don't stack drawers

## Do's and Don'ts

- Do reserve the primary color for the single most important action per screen.
- Do maintain WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1 for body text).
- Don't mix more than two font weights in one view.
- Don't hard-code hex values — reference tokens.
"
